configs=[('homeschool-budget-planner','Free Homeschool Budget Planner: Costs, Payments & PDF','Plan one-time and monthly homeschool costs for one to twelve months. Compare your funding budget, planned costs and payments, export CSV and keep an editable JSON backup.', '''<h2>Plan a homeschool budget without counting shared costs twice</h2><p>Choose a project label, fixed review date, period length from 1 to 12 months and a USD funding budget. Add 1–50 items across curriculum, materials, activities, technology and other costs. Use anonymous learner labels or a shared household group. Enter a shared subscription once; do not repeat its full price for every child unless you really buy separate subscriptions.</p><h3>What each row means</h3><p>Quantity is the number of units per occurrence, from 1 to 100. Unit cost is the cost of one unit. Once means one occurrence in the whole period; monthly multiplies by your selected number of months. Paid to date is the actual total paid for that row so far, not a unit amount. Money entries accept nonnegative USD amounts up to $1,000,000 with at most two decimal places. This short worksheet does not convert currencies or track payment due dates.</p><h3>Formulas and the budget boundary</h3><p>Planned row cost = quantity × unit cost × occurrences. Occurrences are 1 for once, or the selected months for monthly. Total planned cost adds the rows. Planned headroom = funding budget minus planned cost. Budget remaining after payments = funding budget minus recorded payments. Planned cost not yet spent = planned minus paid; a negative value means payments exceed that plan. Actual payments may cover only part of the period, so this difference is not final savings. An entered funding budget is not a verified receipt and these numbers are not a bank balance.</p><h3>Original fictional example</h3><p>For three months and a $900 budget: two $120 curriculum packs cost $240 once; two $15 materials units per month cost $90; a shared $30 monthly activity costs $90; one shared $20 monthly subscription costs $60. Total planned cost is $480 and planned headroom $420. Payments of $240, $30, $30 and $20 total $320. Budget remaining after payments is $580; planned cost not yet spent is $160. These are invented entries, not a typical family budget or a recommendation to buy products.</p><h3>Review before purchasing</h3><p>Record what is included, renewals, delivery costs and the reason a shared item is needed. Update estimates from actual information and retain the original version. A negative planned headroom is a decision to revise the plan or confirm additional resources, not permission to spend. No grants, tax treatment, curriculum quality or homeschool compliance are evaluated by this tool.</p><h3>Save, export and print</h3><p>Entries remain on this page until you choose a JSON backup. Import checks the same-tool format and asks before replacement. CSV contains reviewed row costs and payments with spreadsheet-formula protection. Print / Save PDF uses your browser dialog. The separate two-page US Letter PDF contains a blank six-row budget sheet and the fictional example; it is static, not fillable. Paid-product formats, automatic saving, reminders and synchronization are separate capabilities.</p><p>Combine the budget with the <a href="/journal/homeschool-schedule-multiple-ages/">multiple-age schedule guide</a> and <a href="/tools/homeschool-attendance-log/">attendance log</a>. Spending more does not establish learning progress; keep evidence of actual work separately.</p>'''),('time-blocking-template','Free Weekly Time-Blocking Template: Gaps, Conflicts & PDF','Create a seven-day time-blocking plan with focus, fixed, break and buffer blocks. Check daily overlaps and gaps, export CSV and restore a JSON backup.', '''<h2>Create a weekly time-blocking plan</h2><p>Choose a Monday week-start date and a same-day start/end window. The same window applies to all seven days, including weekends. Add 1–60 named blocks and select the weekday and type: focus, fixed, break or buffer. Every block must have a positive duration inside the daily window. Overnight blocks are not supported. A weekday with no entries has its whole window free, which does not mean every free minute is available for work.</p><h3>How this differs from the daily builder</h3><p>This worksheet keeps a seven-day block template with a Monday date and block categories. The <a href="/tools/daily-schedule-builder/">daily schedule builder</a> handles one fixed day. The <a href="/tools/printable-planner-builder/">printable layout builder</a> creates writing layouts. None of these promises calendar synchronization, automatic reminders or task-duration predictions.</p><h3>Formulas and overlapping blocks</h3><p>For each weekday, occupied minutes are the union of its entered intervals. Free minutes equal daily-window length minus occupied minutes. Duplicate task minutes equal summed block durations minus occupied minutes. Blocks touching at an endpoint do not overlap. With several simultaneous blocks, duplicate minutes can exceed the length of one conflict. Type totals sum each entered block duration; they can count overlapping promises more than once and must not be treated as unique occupied time.</p><h3>Fictional weekly example</h3><p>In a 09:00–17:00 window, Monday focus 09:00–10:30, a fixed call 10:00–11:00 and lunch 12:00–12:30 sum to 180 block minutes. Their union is 150 minutes, leaving 330 free and 30 duplicate minutes. A Tuesday 14:00–15:00 buffer occupies 60 minutes and leaves 420 free. The other five days are unplanned, each with 480 free window minutes. Weekly totals are 210 occupied, 3,150 free and 30 duplicate minutes across all seven days. Resolve Monday's conflict before committing to both tasks.</p><h3>Use blocks as decisions, not proof of completion</h3><p>Include preparation, travel, breaks and handoffs. Put realistic task scope inside a focus block and identify what can move if a fixed commitment changes. A reserved buffer is already occupied in this worksheet; remove or resize it before allocating the same time elsewhere. A block does not prove the task was completed, and this tool does not check staff qualifications or other people's availability.</p><h3>Keep an editable version and printable copy</h3><p>Review after every edit; the previous report is cleared until you review again. CSV contains the reviewed weekly entries; a same-tool JSON backup restores editable inputs after confirmation. Entries are not saved automatically or sent by this tool to a server. Print / Save PDF prints the current reviewed report. The separate two-page landscape US Letter PDF has blank Monday–Wednesday and Thursday–Sunday columns with a 09:00–17:00 writing grid. It is static, not fillable, and does not resize to your custom window.</p><p>Use the <a href="/journal/student-planner-guide/">student guide</a> for deadlines, <a href="/journal/homeschool-schedule-multiple-ages/">multi-age homeschool guide</a> for shared and individual time, or <a href="/journal/consulting-business-plan/">consulting plan</a> for delivery capacity. Keep sensitive personal details out of shared block titles.</p>''')]
for slug,title,desc,guide in configs:
 s=t.replace('daily-schedule-builder',slug).replace('data-day3','data-day4').replace('d3-','d4-').replace('day3-planning-tools','day4-planning-tools').replace('20261106','20261107').replace('November 6, 2026','November 7, 2026')
 old='Free Daily Schedule Builder: Time Blocks &amp; Overlap Check';s=s.replace(old,html.escape(title)).replace('Free Daily Schedule Builder: Time Blocks & Overlap Check',title)
 s=re.sub(r'<meta name="description" content="[^"]*">',f'<meta name="description" content="{html.escape(desc)}">',s)
 s=s.replace('Plan your day with exact time blocks and identify duplicate time promises.','Plan shared and individual learning costs for a fixed period, then compare them with recorded payments.' if slug=='homeschool-budget-planner' else 'Plan a whole week with named blocks, realistic gaps and visible conflicts.')
 a=s.index('<form id="d4-form">');b=s.index('<button type="submit">',a)
 fields='<div class="d1-grid"><label>Project label (required)<input id="d4-name" maxlength="100" required></label><label>'+('Fixed review date' if slug=='homeschool-budget-planner' else 'Week starting Monday')+' (required)<input id="d4-asof" type="date" required></label>'
 fields+='<label>Period months (1–12)<input id="d4-months" type="number" min="1" max="12" step="1" value="3" required></label><label>Funding budget for the whole period (USD)<input id="d4-funding" inputmode="decimal" maxlength="10" value="0" required></label>' if slug=='homeschool-budget-planner' else '<label>Daily window start<input id="d4-start" type="time" required></label><label>Daily window end<input id="d4-end" type="time" required></label>'
 fields+='</div><div id="d4-rows"></div><button id="d4-add" type="button">Add '+('item' if slug=='homeschool-budget-planner' else 'block')+'</button>'
 s=s[:a]+'<form id="d4-form">'+fields+s[b:]
 a=s.index('<h2>Build a realistic daily schedule');b=s.index('</section></main>',a);s=s[:a]+guide+s[b:]
 # Old generated SEO is removed and rebuilt from the new canonical metadata.
 s=re.sub(r'<script id="nexaly-seo" type="application/ld\+json">.*?</script>','',s,flags=re.S)
 p=R/'tools'/slug/'index.html';p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_text(s)
(R/'assets/css/day4-planning-tools.css').write_text((R/'assets/css/day3-planning-tools.css').read_text().replace('d3-','d4-')+'\n.d4-row legend{font-weight:700}.d4-row button{align-self:end}@media print{.d1-report p{overflow-wrap:anywhere}}\n')
pdfmetrics.registerFont(TTFont('D4','/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf'));pdfmetrics.registerFont(TTFont('D4B','/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf'))
ink=HexColor('#203d4a');teal=HexColor('#176c66');line=HexColor('#c4d4d0')
def header(c,title,sub,w,h,pg):
 c.setFillColor(teal);c.rect(0,h-48,w,48,fill=1,stroke=0);c.setFillColor(HexColor('#ffffff'));c.setFont('D4B',12);c.drawString(36,h-29,'NEXALYPLANNER / FREE WORKSHEET');c.setFillColor(ink);c.setFont('D4B',21);c.drawString(36,h-86,title);c.setFont('D4',9);c.drawString(36,h-110,sub);c.setFont('D4',8);c.drawString(36,24,f'nexalyplanner.com | US Letter | Static writing sheet, not fillable | {pg} / 2')
c=canvas.Canvas(str(R/'downloads/homeschool-budget-planner.pdf'),pagesize=letter);c.setTitle('Homeschool Budget Planner - Blank and Fictional Example');c.setAuthor('NexalyPlanner')
for pg in [1,2]:
 header(c,'Homeschool budget planner','Blank period budget' if pg==1 else 'Fictional example: three months, USD; assumptions only.',612,792,pg)
 c.setFont('D4',10);c.drawString(36,648,'Project: _______________________  Review date: ___________________');c.drawString(36,624,'Months: ______  Funding budget (USD): ___________________________')
 for x,label in [(42,'Item / group'),(273,'Frequency'),(356,'Qty'),(392,'Unit $'),(457,'Plan $'),(518,'Paid $')]:c.drawString(x,590,label)
 rows=[('Curriculum / 2 learners','once','2','120','240','240'),('Materials / 2 learners','monthly','2','15','90','30'),('Activity / shared','monthly','1','30','90','30'),('Technology / shared','monthly','1','20','60','20')]
 c.setStrokeColor(line)
 for i in range(6):
  y=562-i*46;c.line(36,y-20,576,y-20)
  if pg==2 and i<len(rows):
   c.setFont('D4',8)
   for x,value in zip([42,273,356,392,457,518],rows[i]):c.drawString(x,y,value)
 c.setFont('D4',10)
 notes=['Planned cost: '+('$480' if pg==2 else '________')+'    Paid to date: '+('$320' if pg==2 else '________'), 'Planned headroom: '+('$420' if pg==2 else '________')+'    Budget after payments: '+('$580' if pg==2 else '________'), 'Planned cost not yet spent: '+('$160' if pg==2 else '________'), 'Row plan = quantity x unit cost x occurrences (1 or selected months).','Enter shared costs once. Payments are row totals paid so far.','Budget differences are not bank cash, final savings or learning outcomes.']
 for i,n in enumerate(notes):c.drawString(36,244-i*25,n)
